  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'navajo-pearl-sterling-silver-turquoise-necklace-hand-strung-by-native-american-a', '4296957961', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/4296957961/navajo-sterling-silver-pearls-kingman?click_key=EugH2sedQ8DY96Hl5Iy7rAo3RF6b%3ALTb68868e91de8d612235037cff52f7ec71f81f6e5&click_sum=5a01e6fd&ls=a&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=Navajo+jewelry&ref=search_grid-72798-17-2&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&pro=1&frs=1&sts=1',
   'NAVAJO Pearl Sterling Silver Turquoise Necklace Hand-Strung by Native American Artisans', 'Style 10 NAVAJO Pearl Style Sterling Silver Pearls with Kingman Turquoise Nuggets on this beautiful Necklace. The pearls are 3-8mm in size and Oxidized Pearl Beads are Hand-Strung by Navajo artisans in Gallup, New Mexico! These necklaces pair well with your Navajo Pearls and other Native American jewelry. NOTE: The clasp is a shepherd''s hook and there is a sterling silver .925 quality tag attached...See Pics! Choose your desired length at checkout. Our sterling silver pearl necklaces are hand-strung and designed by Navajo jewelry artists using machine-made Sterling Silver beads which the artists oxidize and hand-finish to a beautiful patina. Navajo Pearls come in varying pearl sizes, lengths, and patterns. They are beautiful worn alone or with pendants of varying sizes. The Navajo artists who string our Navajo Pearls work in Northwestern New Mexico near the Navajo Nation. The silver has been acid-tested on a jeweler’s stone and verified as sterling silver (.925). Navajo Artist Group from Gallup, NM 16" Length Price: $195.00 18" Length Price: $205.00 20" Length Price: $219.00 22” Length Price: $239.00 24” Length Price: $259.00 Ships FREE FOLLOW ME at https://www.facebook.com/BlueRockTurquoise to stay updated on new additions to our shop AND fun pics of our crazy lives... Our mission is to inspire a revolution of LOVE for handmade Native American Turquoise (and other stones) Jewelry! Join us in our OBSESSION for this beautiful and well-made jewelry. My sister and I (Kim and Phyllis) lived in Cloudcroft, NM as children. Phyllis and her husband Craig own Burro Street Trading Post in Cloudcroft and have a LIVE Facebook Jewelry show most Tuesdays at 6:00 p.m. Mountain Time. I manage the ETSY site for shoppers who prefer to shop online. Phyllis and Craig host the LIVE Facebook shows...and I make guest appearances! Come join us on Tuesday evenings for a fun-filled event featuring authentic Native American jewelry at https://www.facebook.com/BurroStreetTradingPost. Authentic', 'statement-pieces',
